  clock: 2  # 7897
  nonce: '7897'  # 7897
  message: "From WI-nakur's branch (jgstern-agent/fix/nakur, not merged), facts that bear on this item:\n\n1. More unregistered Edge.meta keys, not in the 34 listed: scip/edges.py writes scip_src_symbol, scip_dst_symbol, scip_relationship_flag; scip/calls.py writes scip_src_symbol, scip_dst_symbol, symbol_roles. axis_meta_keys registers only scip_kind (symbol meta). Checked by grep, not by a survey count (no relationship edges in any recorded run, so the edges.py keys have 0 occurrences today).\n2. The new hypergumbo_core.value_flow can enumerate dict KEYS: ModuleValueFlow(tree).resolve(expr, ((\"key\",),)) returns the keys of a dict display plus subscript-store / setdefault / update keys. Probe: meta={\"k1\": 1, \"k2\": 2} -> {'k1', 'k2'}. BUT a named dict passed as meta=edge_meta resolves to None: its escape rule counts the Edge.create(meta=...) call itself as an escape (the constructor is not a known non-mutating callee). A meta-key linter built on it must exempt the sink use (or resolve from the dict's own binding).\n3. Shapes that still hide values from the producer gates (statement-level narrowing, cross-module helpers, nested mutable collections) are listed on WI-gajoz-fasad-vojih-gomup-domar-zivis-durok-rudin; the same limits will apply to meta keys."  # 7897
